.env
# AI 运行态文件（不入库，AGENTS.md §5）
/memory.md
/record.md
/project-progress.html

.gocache
.tmp
tools
bin/
coverage.*
docs/evidence/*
!docs/evidence/*.md
# Raw pprof captures are the evidence behind docs/evidence/pprof_report_*.md.
# Without them the report's CPU/heap claims cannot be re-derived by a reader,
# and a report citing a path that is not in the checkout is a phantom reference.
#
# The directory must be re-included before its contents: git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so a file rule alone does nothing while
# `docs/evidence/*` still excludes the directory itself. Measured - with only
# the file rule, cpu.prof stayed ignored.
#
# Contents are then excluded again and only the capture formats re-included, so
# an unrelated artifact dropped into this directory is not swept in by accident.
# Measured: with a bare `pprof-*/*`, random.bin and sub/evil.bin were both
# trackable - wider than this rule claims to be.
!docs/evidence/pprof-*/
docs/evidence/pprof-*/*
!docs/evidence/pprof-*/*.prof
!docs/evidence/pprof-*/*.txt

# Tool-generated atomic-write backups (for example, config.go.123456789).
*.go.[0-9]*
*.log
*.dump
erl_crash.dump
